      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140514_19051666_0252.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140514_19051666_0252&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140514_19051666_0252.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140514_19052539_0253.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140514_19052539_0253&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140514_19052539_0253.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From: Ralph A.H., To: Grace Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Griggsville, Delaware on September 2, 1909&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Miss Grace Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Pearl, Illinois&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Am in Griggsville. Am not sure when I will leave. Please write and tell me of all your big doings. Nothing stirring for me here.&lt;br&gt;
Ralph A.H.&lt;br&gt;
9/2/09&lt;br&gt;
Griggsville, Delaware&lt;/p&gt;</description>
